.TH rev-stealth-hermes-install 1  "rev-stealth-hermes-install " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-hermes\-install \- Install the Hermes plugin scaffold into `<prefix>`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth hermes install\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install the bundled Hermes MCP plugin scaffold into <prefix> (default: $HOME/.hermes/plugins/rev\-scraping\-mcp). \-\-source overrides the scaffold origin. \-\-force overwrites a non\-empty destination.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: side\-effect\-free plan emission. No file writes, no network calls, no keyring operations. Returns exit 0 after emitting the structured plan envelope
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: include the action plan in the result envelope\*(Aqs `result.plan` field. Can be combined with `\-\-dry\-run`. When passed without `\-\-dry\-run`, the plan is emitted alongside the real action
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5 / G.6: opaque caller\-supplied key for at\-most\-once commit semantics. Accepted in G.5; surfaced in the envelope; the underlying commit replay semantics land in G.6
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR
Destination directory. Defaults to `$HOME/.hermes/plugins/rev\-scraping\-mcp`
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<SOURCE>\fR
Override the scaffold source directory (defaults to the `dist/hermes/rev\-scraping\-mcp` shipped with the repo)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite an existing non\-empty destination
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth hermes install
  $ rev\-stealth hermes install \-\-prefix /opt/hermes/plugins/rev\-scraping\-mcp
  $ rev\-stealth hermes install \-\-force \-\-source ./dist/hermes/rev\-scraping\-mcp

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Install completed.
  1  UserError        Destination non\-empty (use \-\-force) / bad \-\-source.
  3  PermanentError   scaffold IO failure.

ENV:
  (none consumed directly; respects HOME for default \-\-prefix.)
